[0.134, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mThe\u001b[7Glink\u001b[12Gcheck\u001b[18Gfinds\u001b[24Gno\u001b[27Gbroken\u001b[34Glinks\u001b[40Gacross\u001b[47Gthe\u001b[51G22\u001b[54GMarkdown\u001b[63Gfiles,\u001b[70Gand\u001b[74Gshellcheck\u001b[85Greports\u001b[93Gnothing\u001b[101Gin\u001b[104Geither\u001b[111Gscript.\r\u001b[1B  Next I'm running the full gate, after checking free memory first.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Interrupted · What should Claude do instead?\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mI restarted you\u001b[39m                                                                                                       \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[24G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[39m The restart stopped the previous gate partway through its unit tests. Nothing is running now and 54 GiB is free, so\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  I'm running the gate again.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mDoes the script you wrote remind me to exit the asciinema shell once I exit claude? I think a one line reminder to \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mCTRL-D out of that shell would be very useful.\u001b[39m                                                                        \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mThe script's \u001b[38;2;177;185;249masciinema rec\u001b[39m command ends\u001b[43Gthe recordin\u001b[56G when\u001b[62GClaude\u001b[69GCode\u001b[74Gexits,\u001b[81Gso\u001b[84GCtrl-D\u001b[91Gisn't\u001b[97Gneeded.\u001b[105GI'll\u001b[110Greport\u001b[117Gwhen\r\u001b[1B  the gate finishes.\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · summa\u001b[30Gy\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[4B\u001b[38;2;233;154;122mHatching…\r\u001b[